--- A function handed a list of vectors (`[i, i]`, a collect's pairs) and a
--- list of lists (rows grown by `push`) is copied for each, as they are
--- held two ways: one copy had taken both, and the call handing the other
--- disagreed with itself (Rosetta Code, Cartesian product).
fn shown[rows]
    return len[rows]

pairs = for i in range[2]
    [i, i]
log[shown[pairs]]
rows = push[[], push[[], 7]]
log[shown[rows]]
